Hi Chris,

First of all, thank you for your kind reply and information.
And when I look at those links, I am very interested in 15 inch CGA EGA 
VGA to XGA LCD panel (00472).
But I want you to make sure that we can use that LCD monitor to replace 
our current KME CGA CRT monitor.
Here for your review I send you the information  for our current monitor.

And one more thing if we go with RGB-CGA, EGA, HD to VGA converter then I 
wonder if it is still possible solution for our purpose to replace the 
current CRT monitor.
If it is another possible solution, please give me price information for 
that converter too.

Then I will wait for your confirmation and also we wonder how you are 
going to ship it to us in US.
Thank you again.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
This monitor uses a TTL video input and TTL level sync input at 15.63Khz 
(Horizontal rate) and 50.08hz (vertical rate) through the 9 way 'D' socket 
on rear of monitor.
 
The monitor connector is wired as follows:
 

 
The monitor will operate on 110v/240v (auto-ranging).

